The  interface  captures IPv6 TCP traffic, for implementing user‐
land IPv6‐to‐IPv4 TCP relay like Special  action  will  be  taken
when IPv6 TCP traffic is seen on a router, and routing table sug‐
gests to route it to interface.  In this case, the packet will be
accepted  by the router, regardless of list of IPv6 interface ad‐
dresses assigned to the router.  The packet will be  captured  by
an  IPv6 TCP socket, if it has flag turned on and it has matching
address/port pairs.  In result, will let  you  capture  IPv6  TCP
traffic  to  some  specific destination addresses.  Userland pro‐
grams, such as can use this behavior to relay IPv6 TCP traffic to
IPv4 TCP traffic.  The program can accept some specific IPv6  TCP
traffic, perform to get the IPv6 destination address specified by
the  client,  and perform application‐specific address mapping to
relay IPv6 TCP to IPv4 TCP.  The flag on IPv6 TCP socket  can  be
set by using with level equals to and optname equals to To handle
error  reports by ICMPv6, some of ICMPv6 packets routed to inter‐
face will be delivered to IPv6 TCP, as well.  To  understand  how
